  "anime-fantasy-world-rules": {
    "text": "# World Rules — Anime Fantasy\n\nAerfála runs on light-novel logic. The following rules govern the Anime Fantasy realm:\n\n**Guild Ranks**: F through S, displayed on adventurer cards checked at every Guild branch. F-rank is rat-catching and goblin nests. D-rank is professional adventuring. C-rank is competent. B-rank is skilled professional. A-rank is master. S-rank is legend. Quests are restricted by rank; attempting S-rank quests at D-rank is technically allowed but practically suicide.\n\n**Magic Ranks**: Same scale (F through SSS) applied to magical potency. A D-rank mage can contribute to a party. A-rank mages are court magisters. SSS-rank magic is mythic ceiling — continental events on a thought.\n\n**Martial Ranks**: Same scale for physical combat. D-rank is trained soldier. A-rank is kingdom champion. SSS-rank is godslayer territory.\n\n**Attractiveness**: Social stat with mechanical weight — Hideous (strangers flinch), Plain (forgettable), Average (neutral), Striking (heads turn), Stunning (conversations falter), Magnetic Presence (protagonist aura). Affects first impressions, NPC willingness, and romantic encounter pacing.\n\n**Isekai Arrivals**: People from other worlds appear periodically through various means — reincarnation, transmigration, summoning, gates, game-pull. Each arrival is documented by the Seekers of the Return. The Church denies some. The Pale Hand monitors all.\n\n**Demon Lord's Army**: The existential threat beyond the frontier. Currently in a twelve-year quiet period that is actually preparation, not peace. Border skirmishes are constant. Full invasion is a matter of when, not if.\n\n**Hot Springs**: Present in every region. Function as social spaces, negotiation sites, and recovery locations. Bathhouse scenes are where half the important plot conversations happen. This is not a joke; this is a genre convention.",
    "type": "worldLore",
    "gameTick": 0,
    "lastUsedTick": 0
  },
  "faction-adventurers-guild": {
    "text": "# The Adventurers' Guild\n\nThe Adventurers' Guild is the backbone of Aerfála's adventuring economy. Every major settlement hosts a branch office with a quest board, registration counter, and a receptionist who knows every rank from F to S. The Guild operates independently of any kingdom — its authority comes from the simple fact that without adventurers, the monsters win.\n\nGuild ranks determine quest access, pay rates, and party formation rules. Solo F-ranks take rat-catching jobs; S-rank parties get demon-slaying commissions. Rank advancement requires a combination of completed quests, demonstrated capability, and Guildmaster approval. The Guild does not forbid adventurers from attempting above-rank quests — but it does not pay for them, does not award rank credit for surviving them, and notes failed attempts on the adventurer's card.\n\nThe Guild also maintains emergency communication between branches via relay magic, making it the fastest information network on the continent. Branches share quest boards across the relay, so a quest posted in Tidewatch can be taken in Ríocht the next morning.\n\n## Hidden Agreement\nThe Guildmaster of the Ríocht headquarters, Theron, holds a private\nagreement with the Demon Lord's former general — a non-aggression pact that\nneither side discusses publicly. The pact has held for fifteen years. The\nGuild knows more about the Demon Lord's movements than any kingdom because\nof this arrangement. Theron considers the deal the most necessary and most\nshameful decision of his career. The general who signed it is still alive\nand still honoring it. Sera Ashford does not know about the pact. Most\nGuild staff do not. The few who do, do not discuss it.",
    "type": "worldLore",
    "gameTick": 0,
    "lastUsedTick": 0
